{{!
    @template enrol_apply/course_group_mode

    The first row of the instance form's Groups section: the course's group mode, what it means for
    who decides an application, and a link to the course settings where the mode is changed, for a
    reader who may change them. Every value arrives in its plain spelling: the double stashes
    escape them.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * mode string - the group mode's name, as core words it
    * consequence string - one sentence on who sees an application in that mode
    * hasurl boolean - whether the reader may open the course settings
    * url string - the course settings page
    * linktext string - the link's text

    Example context (json):
    {
        "mode": "Separate groups",
        "consequence": "An application with a group reaches the deciders of that group, and those who see every group.",
        "hasurl": true,
        "url": "https://example.com/course/edit.php?id=2",
        "linktext": "Change it in the course settings"
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-groupmode">
    <strong>{{mode}}</strong>
    <div>{{consequence}}</div>
    {{#hasurl}}
        <div><a href="{{url}}">{{linktext}}</a></div>
    {{/hasurl}}
</div>
